g of all objects with the wrong __module__ attribute.","doc_summary":"Returns a mapping of all objects with the wrong __module__ attribute."},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_public_api.is_unexpected","kind":"function","dispname":"is_unexpected","docUri":null,"signature":"(name)","doc":"Check if this needs to be considered.","doc_summary":"Check if this needs to be considered."},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_public_api.np","kind":"package","dispname":"np","docUri":"https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/index.html#module-numpy","signature":null,"doc_summary":"NumPy","aliasOf":"numpy"},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_public_api.numpy","kind":"package","dispname":"numpy","docUri":"https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/index.html#module-numpy","signature":null,"doc_summary":"NumPy","aliasOf":"numpy"},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_public_api.run_subprocess","kind":"function","dispname":"run_subprocess","docUri":null,"signature":"(cmd, cwd=None, **kwargs)","doc_summary":"Run ``cmd`` in a subprocess, failing the test with its captured output if it exits with a nonzero status.","aliasOf":"numpy.testing._private.utils.run_subprocess"},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_public_api.test_NPY_NO_EXPORT","kind":"function","dispname":"test_NPY_NO_EXPORT","docUri":null,"signature":"()"},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_public_api.test___module___attribute","kind":"function","dispname":"test___module___attribute","docUri":null,"signature":"()"},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_public_api.test___qualname___and___module___attribute","kind":"function","dispname":"test___qualname___and___module___attribute","docUri":null,"signature":"()"},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_public_api.test_all_modules_are_expected","kind":"function","dispname":"test_all_modules_are_expected","docUri":null,"signature":"()","doc":"Test that we don't add anything that looks like a new public module by\naccident.  Check is based on filenames.","doc_summary":"Test that we don't add anything that looks like a new public module by accident.  Check is based on filenames."},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_public_api.test_all_modules_are_expected_2","kind":"function","dispname":"test_all_modules_are_expected_2","docUri":null,"signature":"()","doc":"Method checking all objects. The pkgutil-based method in\n`test_all_modules_are_expected` does not catch imports into a namespace,\nonly filenames.  So this test is more thorough, and checks this like:\n\n    import .lib.scimath as emath\n\nTo check if something in a module is (effectively) public, one can check if\nthere's anything in that namespace that's a public function/object but is\nnot exposed in a higher-level namespace.  For example for a `numpy.lib`\nsubmodule::\n\n    mod = np.lib.mixins\n    for obj in mod.__all__:\n        if obj in np.__all__:\n            continue\n        elif obj in np.lib.__all__:\n            continue\n\n        else:\n            print(obj)","doc_summary":"Method checking all objects. The pkgutil-based method in `test_all_modules_are_expected` does not catch imports into a namespace, only filenames.  So this test is more thorough, and checks this like:"},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_public_api.test_api_importable","kind":"function","dispname":"test_api_importable","docUri":null,"signature":"()","doc":"Check that all submodules listed higher up in this file can be imported\n\nNote that if a PRIVATE_BUT_PRESENT_MODULES entry goes missing, it may\nsimply need to be removed from the list (deprecation may or may not be\nneeded - apply common sense).","doc_summary":"Check that all submodules listed higher up in this file can be imported"},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_public_api.test_array_api_entry_point","kind":"function","dispname":"test_array_api_entry_point","docUri":null,"signature":"()","doc":"Entry point for Array API implementation can be found with importlib and\nreturns the main numpy namespace.","doc_summary":"Entry point for Array API implementation can be found with importlib and returns the main numpy namespace."},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_public_api.test_core_shims_coherence","kind":"function","dispname":"test_core_shims_coherence","docUri":null,"signature":"()","doc":"Check that all \"semi-public\" members of `numpy._core` are also accessible\nfrom `numpy.core` shims.","doc_summary":"Check that all \"semi-public\" members of `numpy._core` are also accessible from `numpy.core` shims."},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_public_api.test_dir_testing","kind":"function","dispname":"test_dir_testing","docUri":null,"signature":"()","doc":"Assert that output of dir has only one \"testing/tester\"\nattribute without duplicate","doc_summary":"Assert that output of dir has only one \"testing/tester\" attribute without duplicate"},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_public_api.test_functions_single_location","kind":"function","dispname":"test_functions_single_location","docUri":null,"signature":"()","doc":"Check that each public function is available from one location only.\n\nTest performs BFS search traversing NumPy's public API. It flags\nany function-like object that is accessible from more that one place.","doc_summary":"Check that each public function is available from one location only."},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_public_api.test_import_lazy_import","kind":"function","dispname":"test_import_lazy_import","docUri":null,"signature":"(name)","doc":"Make sure we can actually use the modules we lazy load.\n\nWhile not exported as part of the public API, it was accessible.  With the\nuse of __getattr__ and __dir__, this isn't always true It can happen that\nan infinite recursion may happen.\n\nThis is the only way I found that would force the failure to appear on the\nbadly implemented code.\n\nWe also test for the presence of the lazily imported modules in dir","doc_summary":"Make sure we can actually use the modules we lazy load."},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_public_api.test_main_namespace_all_dir_coherence","kind":"function","dispname":"test_main_namespace_all_dir_coherence","docUri":null,"signature":"()","doc":"Checks if `dir(np)` and