pname":"test_warnings","docUri":null,"signature":null,"doc":"Tests which scan for certain occurrences in the code, they may not find\nall of these occurrences but should catch almost all.","doc_summary":"Tests which scan for certain occurrences in the code, they may not find all of these occurrences but should catch almost all."},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_warnings.FindFuncs","kind":"class","dispname":"FindFuncs","docUri":null,"signature":"(filename)","doc":"A node visitor base class that walks the abstract syntax tree and calls a\nvisitor function for every node found.  This function may return a value\nwhich is forwarded by the `visit` method.\n\nThis class is meant to be subclassed, with the subclass adding visitor\nmethods.\n\nPer default the visitor functions for the nodes are ``'visit_'`` +\nclass name of the node.  So a `TryFinally` node visit function would\nbe `visit_TryFinally`.  This behavior can be changed by overriding\nthe `visit` method.  If no visitor function exists for a node\n(return value `None`) the `generic_visit` visitor is used instead.\n\nDon't use the `NodeVisitor` if you want to apply changes to nodes during\ntraversing.  For this a special visitor exists (`NodeTransformer`) that\nallows modifications.","doc_summary":"A node visitor base class that walks the abstract syntax tree and calls a visitor function for every node found.  This function may return a value which is forwarded by the `visit` method."},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_warnings.ParseCall","kind":"class","dispname":"ParseCall","docUri":null,"signature":"()","doc":"A node visitor base class that walks the abstract syntax tree and calls a\nvisitor function for every node found.  This function may return a value\nwhich is forwarded by the `visit` method.\n\nThis class is meant to be subclassed, with the subclass adding visitor\nmethods.\n\nPer default the visitor functions for the nodes are ``'visit_'`` +\nclass name of the node.  So a `TryFinally` node visit function would\nbe `visit_TryFinally`.  This behavior can be changed by overriding\nthe `visit` method.  If no visitor function exists for a node\n(return value `None`) the `generic_visit` visitor is used instead.\n\nDon't use the `NodeVisitor` if you want to apply changes to nodes during\ntraversing.  For this a special visitor exists (`NodeTransformer`) that\nallows modifications.","doc_summary":"A node visitor base class that walks the abstract syntax tree and calls a visitor function for every node found.  This function may return a value which is forwarded by the `visit` method."},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_warnings.__builtins__","kind":"variable","dispname":"__builtins__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_warnings.__cached__","kind":"constant","dispname":"__cached__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_warnings.__doc__","kind":"constant","dispname":"__doc__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_warnings.__file__","kind":"constant","dispname":"__file__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_warnings.__loader__","kind":"variable","dispname":"__loader__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_warnings.__name__","kind":"constant","dispname":"__name__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_warnings.__package__","kind":"constant","dispname":"__package__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_warnings.__spec__","kind":"variable","dispname":"__spec__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_warnings.numpy","kind":"package","dispname":"numpy","docUri":"https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/index.html#module-numpy","signature":null,"doc_summary":"NumPy","aliasOf":"numpy"},{"path":"numpy.tests.test_warnings.test_warning_calls","kind":"function","dispname":"test_warning_calls","docUri":null,"signature":"()"}]}
